2026-10-31T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2391) '- Guests at double, in &{repo("contract-guest-runtime")}'s vendored sandbox-api: `target_compile_definitions(sandbox_api PUBLIC DOUBLE_PRECISION_REAL_T)` under the option; `node2d.cpp` returns `real_t`; `vector.cpp`'s wrappers take `real_t`, checked against the host's `ECALL_VEC3_OPS` handler in the placed source for what `fa0` carries. The pen's `build.sh` passes `-DDOUBLE_PRECISION=ON`. Xgodot_lite` stays float, since the host boundary is `api.hpp`'s `Variant` and `PackedFloat32Array` is float either way. `lasso` and `curvenet` export `variant_bytes()`.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2391  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2391) '- A Mojo guest is held to the same size. It names 40 bytes in its own `.sandbox_variant` section and the double host refuses a guest that names another (RFD66606-2494, operator, 2026-11-14).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2391  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2391) '- Superseded for the beta (operator, 2026-11-25). The beta runs on stock Godot 4.8-beta5 at single precision with the godot-sandbox addon, and the engine fork goes to the archive. A guest builds at both precisions and releases both, and the beta loads the single ELF, whose `.sandbox_variant` names 24 bytes. Double precision returns when a feature needs it.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2391  1 LINE
 Text:Written

